Subject: [PATCH] playerbots: a bot standing in a zone with no grind spot or hub picks one from a neighbouring zone

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

NewRpgBaseAction::SelectRandomGrindPos and ::SelectRandomCampPos
(src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp, at the pin) keep a cached
destination only when the zone at that destination equals the bot's own zone
(unless the bot stands in a capital). A bot whose own zone caches nothing then
has no grind spot and no camp: the strategy's other statuses are unavailable
too (quest points are zone-filtered the same way), RandomChangeStatus finds no
available status, and it takes the "all unavailable" branch, which sets the bot
to REST and sits it down. Nothing later changes that, because the bot's zone
does not change while it sits.

Measured on the dev realm on 2026-11-15, from Playerbots.log and the
characters table: of 197 bots online on map 530, 31 of the 32 standing in zone
3455 (The North Sea) logged only empty grind picks ("Map:4294967295 ... 0+0
available") in the 400000 most recent pick lines, none a valid one. They stand
at the sea surface (z -1.2) west of the Sunstrider Isle, level 1 to 12, up to
609 hours played, and the other 33 characters of that zone are offline there.
The same empty picks are logged by 15 bots in Eversong Woods at level 14 to 16
and by a few in Ghostlands and Azuremyst: a zone with no cached spot at the
bot's level (Eversong's creatures stop around level 10) strands them the same
way. Ghostlands, one zone away, has spots for them.

This adds a second pass to both functions. Only when the first pass (same zone
only, exactly as before) finds nothing does the second pass accept a cached
spot or hub from any zone of the bot's own map, inside the same distance
limits as before (the level 1 to 4 limits are unchanged). A bot that has a
spot in its own zone behaves exactly as before; a bot in a capital is not
affected. No bot is teleported: it walks or swims to the spot like any other.

HOW A BOT GOT INTO THE SEA WAS NOT FOUND. This patch does not stop a bot
entering open water; it makes a bot that is already there able to leave. The
quest-point and wander code were not changed.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

An upstream change that falls back to a neighbouring zone, or to the nearest
spot on the map, when the bot's own zone has none.

APPLIES TO

  repo: https://github.com/quadseven/mod-playerbots.git
  SHA:  40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130 (the pin), and it also
        applies after every local patch in the infra copy of this directory
        (checked with git apply --check, with offsets). It touches only
        NewRpgBaseAction::SelectRandomGrindPos and ::SelectRandomCampPos.

